## 1. How the framework works

| Phase | Trigger in the supplied implementation | Work performed |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Merge-request gate | Feature push and merge request; workflow primary. | Lint, security scan, unit tests, and E2E type check. |
| Device execution | Merge to main or master; deploy-android or deploy-ios. | Build Release APK/IPA, upload, run selected device tests, and publish JUnit/HTML and a Sauce link. |
| Notifications | End of the deploy workflow, when enabled. | Teams or email receives pass/fail and a build reference. |
| Developer checks | Local bootstrap and pipeline commands, when provided by the project. | Prepare the environment and run the local checks. |

Confirm actual workflow names and triggers in your selected shared template. The reference estimates 2–3 hours for first-app setup and about 30 minutes for later apps; access and queue time affect those estimates. Its rollout plan is included in section 11.

