## 10. Security rules

Keep .env, .vault/secrets.env, .provision.env, keystores, .p12 files, provisioning profiles, populated buildEnv.ts, and token-bearing Teams URLs out of commits. Secrets belong in the approved CI bindings and ERPM/local approved secret storage. Rotate a leaked value before cleaning up its copies and history.

The source security script scans secret hygiene and reports npm audit findings for review. Its lint script skips lint if ESLint is absent. Check which checks actually executed. Review high/critical dependency findings each release. Protect default-branch writes and require passing configured checks and review.

The source fixture exposes TEST_PASSWORD to PRs and keeps Sauce credentials out of them. Platform owners confirm the applicable trust settings. Expiring provisioning tokens are revoked or removed after setup.

